{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>ובאה</b> The word אחותי את. As above, because the reason is in the word following it, the first letter [takes] a kamatz gadol, and likewise קָרָא לָילָה (Genesis 1:5), and this is the rule of the language. And the dagesh of the tav in אָת is because of the assimilation of the nun, for it is from the root אני." "<b>בגללך.</b> And 'on your account.' They come only with a bet. And the one who removes the bet is one who lacks understanding." "And the meaning of ייטב לי: a gift and offering, and likewise it is written ולאברם היטיב בעבורה (Genesis 12:16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:23.395303896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}